========================================================================
SCALE / PERFORMANCE (core OWN)
========================================================================

### A. Module chain (linear import depth)

Fixtures: `/tmp/r2_peer2_scale/c{N}/` — leaf `m_a.oo` … chain to letter N;
main imports last. **Names avoid digit `0`.**

| N | modules (+main) | raw sum B | check rc | times (s, 3 runs) | median-ish |
|---|-----------------|-----------|----------|-------------------|------------|
| 2 | 3 | 160 | 0 OK | 0.05 0.05 0.07 | ~0.05 |
| 5 | 6 | 349 | 0 OK | 0.05 0.06 0.10 | ~0.06 |
| 10 | 11 | 664 | 0 OK | 0.13 0.14 0.13 | ~0.13 |
| 20 | 21 | 1294 | 0 OK | 0.52 0.48 0.60 | ~0.52 |

**Honesty:** sub-second on **tiny** bodies. Growth is super-linear-ish
(N=10→20 ~4× time for 2× modules) but still small absolute. **Not** evidence
that product-scale trees are fine.

### B. Fan-out (main imports N siblings)

Fixtures: `/tmp/r2_peer2_scale/fanL{N}/`.

| N | check rc | times (s, 3 runs) |
|---|----------|-------------------|
| 2 | 0 OK | 0.06 0.07 0.07 |
| 5 | 0 OK | 0.18 0.17 0.19 |
| 10 | 0 OK | 0.71 0.32 0.26 |
| 20 | 0 OK | 1.25 0.94 1.06 |

Fan-out costs more than depth chain at same N (more symbols in one expanded
stream). Still ≤ ~1.3s for N=20 toy modules.

